---
import R1 from '../assets/screens/R1.png';
import R2 from '../assets/screens/R2.png';
import R3 from '../assets/screens/R3.png';
import PageHeader from '../components/PageHeader.astro';
import Section from '../components/Section.astro';
import StillSequence from '../components/StillSequence.astro';
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import styles from './solutions.module.css';
---

<BaseLayout title="Poker Assistant accuracy" description="Solutions measured under one big blind per hundred hands - so you can study with confidence.">
  <PageHeader marker="Accuracy" title="GTO you can trust" lede="Every shipped preflop solution is measured after it solves. The result: under one big blind per hundred hands of exploitable error." />

  <Section top="sm" bottom="lg" width="content" labelledby="number">
    <div class={styles['block']}>
      <h2 id="number">Measured, not guessed</h2>
      <p>After every preflop solve, Poker Assistant measures how much a perfect opponent could still win against it, seat by seat. Shipped packs land in single-digit milli-big-blinds per game: under one big blind per hundred hands. That is the number that matters - published for every pack, not hidden behind solver jargon.</p>
    </div>
  </Section>

  <Section top="lg" bottom="lg" width="content" labelledby="ladder">
    <div class={styles['block']}>
      <h2 id="ladder">Real poker needs a real raise ladder</h2>
      <p>Push/fold is close enough below 12bb. Above it, it is not. Against a 15bb push/fold strategy, a perfect opponent gains about 190bb/100; at 30bb, about 340bb/100. Our full raise ladder stays under one. That is why the ladder begins at 15bb and push/fold ends at 12bb.</p>
    </div>
  </Section>

  <Section top="lg" bottom="lg" width="content" labelledby="methods">
    <div class={styles['block']}>
      <h2 id="methods">Serious methods. Clear standard.</h2>
      <p>The solver uses published CFR and Monte Carlo methods, exhaustive board enumeration and parallel solving across cores. The proof is not the acronym list: every completed preflop solve is tested for exploitability before it ships.</p>
    </div>
  </Section>

  <Section top="lg" bottom="lg" width="content" labelledby="honest">
    <div class={styles['block']}>
      <h2 id="honest">What we will not fake</h2>
      <p>The builder shows a confidence band while a preflop solve runs, so you can see whether the result has settled. Deal a board and Poker Assistant solves that exact flop, turn or river on demand; its progress display shows work completed, not a made-up accuracy claim. Tournament ICM is not included.</p>
    </div>
    <div class={styles['figure']}>
    <StillSequence frames={[{ src: R1, alt: 'Screenshot of a postflop resolve in progress, reporting a running iteration count rather than a convergence measurement.', label: 'Solving' }, { src: R2, alt: 'Screenshot of the same flop resolved, with a full action ladder and range grid in place of the progress readout.', label: 'Solved' }, { src: R3, alt: 'Screenshot of a second flop re-solved on the same line, confirming the resolve runs independently each time.', label: 'Re-solved' }]} caption="The same postflop line resolving on two different boards, each run reporting its own progress." />
    </div>
  </Section>

  <Section top="lg" bottom="2xl" width="content" labelledby="data">
    <div class={styles['block']}>
      <h2 id="data">Your study data stays yours</h2>
      <p>Poker Assistant stores everything on your device and sends nothing. Read the <a href="/privacy">privacy statement</a> for the full commitment.</p>
    </div>
  </Section>
</BaseLayout>
